  * See hw-report.md: volume-up is PM6150L SID 4, NOT PM6150 SID 0.
  * PMIC access is READ ONLY: the sole MMIO write issues EXT_READL on an
  * observer channel. No PMIC config, IRQ acknowledge or reset writes exist.
+ *
+ * 0208 SDM660 (lavender/whyred, PM660 + PM660L), from the phone's own DTB
+ * (resources/lavender_dtb.bin):
+ *   qcom,spmi@800f000 "qcom,spmi-pmic-arb": core 0x0800f000, chnls
+ *   0x08400000, obsrvr 0x09400000, intr 0x0a400000, cnfg 0x0800a000, ee 0.
+ *   That is PMIC arbiter v2/v3 (Linux spmi-pmic-arb.c): the APID -> PPID
+ *   table is at core + 0x800 + 4 * apid (v5: + 0x900), the core has no
+ *   APID count register (up to 512 APIDs), and an observer channel is at
+ *   obsrvr + 0x1000 * ee + 0x8000 * apid (v5: + 0x10000 * ee + 0x80 * apid).
+ *   Channel registers (CMD 0x00, STATUS 0x08, RDATA0 0x18) and the
+ *   EXT_READL command word are the same as v5.
+ *   pm660@0 power-on@800: pon_1 KPDPWR (KEY_POWER), pon_2 RESIN
